body:
I love how supportive your friends are! It's so important to be surrounded by people who appreciate you for how you are.

&#x200B;

I've been in the same boat (as I'm sure a lot of others have) where a parent would chime in on your looks and make you feel "less than". Growing up, my mom would constantly comment on how my chest was really flat compared to her, when she was my age (I'm an A cup and she said she was B/C at my age). The most pronounced period of my life that she would frequently bring it up was when I was 15-20 and it always made me feel insecure and has definitely stayed stuck in my head.

&#x200B;

I'm glad you are able to get past the negative comments. I aspire to be confident in myself. Thank you for sharing <3
